00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
This video recording is file protection and open file table.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
File protection is also a responsibility of a logical file system.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
One issue related to file sharing is access right management.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:29,000
File owner or the creator of the file should be able to control what can be done and by who.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:39,000
The file system should provide a number of options so that the way in which a particular file is accessed can be controlled.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Typically, a group of users are granted certain access right to a file.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:54,000
We illustrate the file protection using Unix as an example.

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
In Unix, each file has a primary group.

9
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:07,000
When a file is created, it is initially associated with the user's primary group.

10
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Groups are created by the Unix Assistant Administrator.

11
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,000
In Unix, there are three classes of users.

12
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Owner who create the file.

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,000
And other users within the same group as the owner.

14
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
And all the rest.

15
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,000
So we have owner, group and public.

16
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:36,000
So owner, as a site, is the user who create the file.

17
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
And group refers to users who are in the same group as the owner.

18
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
And the public refers to the rest of the users.

19
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Then for each class of user, owner, group and public, there are three protection bits.

20
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Read, write and execute.

21
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
For instance, for this particular file.

22
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,000
So this is the protection piece for the file.

23
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:14,000
And for the user, the owner who created the file will be able to read, write and execute the file.

24
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:22,000
However, for other users within the same group as the owner, they can only read and execute the file.

25
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:29,000
And for all the rest, public, they can only execute the file.

26
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:36,000
And the directory is a special kind of file.

27
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:41,000
So like file, each directory also has nine protection bits.

28
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:49,000
So for directory, read permission means operation to list the content of directory is permitted.

29
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:56,000
And the right permission means operation to modify the content of a directory.

30
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Right. For instance, insert an entry in the directory or delete the entry of a directory is permitted.

31
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,000
So recall directory consists of multiple entries.

32
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:13,000
There's one entry per file and entry contains the file attributes or metadata of the file.

33
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,000
So however, there's something unique to the directory.

34
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:23,000
To assign a directory, then the execution permission is essential.

35
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,000
What does that mean?

36
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:34,000
That basically means if there's no execution permission, then corresponding read and write operation on the directory cannot be performed.

37
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Right. So even though read and write permission is set.

38
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Again, to this particular example, so this indicating this is a directory file.

39
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:49,000
And for this directory file, then the user will be able to read and write the directory.

40
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,000
The execution permission is set.

41
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:56,000
So read means able to list the content of the directory.

42
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:03,000
And then write means able to delete or insert a content entry in the directory.

43
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:09,000
And for other users within the same group, then can only read the directory.

44
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Right. So list the content of the directory.

45
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Right. Again, the execution is set.

46
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Right. So for all others, they cannot do, they cannot perform read or write operation on the directory.

47
